      "content": "It sounds like you are experiencing overwhelming dissociation and grief, where the loss of your sense of identity feels like a death of the person you once were. While the fear that nothing matters is very strong, it's possible that trying to \"find\" yourself is actually part of a necessary grieving process, similar to how one feels empty after losing a loved one. Please talk to a doctor or therapist who can help you distinguish between this emotional pain and a medical breakdown, as they can provide support even when it feels pointless. You deserve care that helps you process this loss without expecting you to rebuild everything from scratch right away.",
